  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who are familiar with or interested in historical racial stereotypes and the performative use of imagery to convey messages of peace and love, particularly in the context of Black representation in early 20th-century media. The meme is designed for an audience that may interpret the image through the lens of historical racial caricatures, potentially reinforcing harmful stereotypes despite the positive text overlay. The intended audience likely includes those who engage with internet memes that juxtapose historical imagery with modern messages, often without critically examining the underlying racial dynamics. The audience may also include those who are unaware of the historical context and the potential harm in the visual presentation of the Black man, which could be seen as exoticizing or stereotyping.",
